 "https://go.nature.com/48Oyz4W", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120908738735325184/FgcIa8Fq?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1066}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120908738735325184/FgcIa8Fq?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 131, "status": 200, "title": "Give biologists the space to be curious, not just better tools", "unwound_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03669-w?utm_source=x&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=nature&linkId=64387159&error=cookies_not_supported&code=782c11df-d0e2-462a-a975-1f748563198a", "url": "https://t.co/cefDT9X4LP"}]}, "id": "2120908733056156159", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 7140, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Technology is making biological studies more powerful than ever. But people are the real force behind discovery, says Edith Heard\n\nhttps://t.co/cefDT9X4LP", "url": "https://x.com/Nature/status/2120908733056156159"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:51:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120907413037445533"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 203, "id": "898983926", "start": 191, "username": "yasemin_sap"}]}, "id": "2120907413037445533", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 5292, "like_count": 39, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Done arguing over which type of molecule got life started, a new wave of researchers are deconstructing what life is, does, and could be — and are even trying to create it themselves. \n\nRead @yasemin_sap's feature on a new era for the research into the origins of life:", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120907413037445533"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:45:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120905803393585340"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Scores of doctors and scientists were elected last week. Will trust in science follow?", "display_url": "statnews.com/2026/11/12/tru…", "end": 215, "expanded_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/trust-in-science-physician-lawmakers-rebuild-belief/", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120841811073642496/d66w8c8T?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120841811073642496/d66w8c8T?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 192, "status": 200, "title": "Newly elected doctors and scientists hope to restore trust in science. It won't be easy", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/12/trust-in-science-physician-lawmakers-rebuild-belief/", "url": "https://t.co/uzaevvYlbH"}]}, "id": "2120905803393585340", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1349, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Last week, doctors and scientists across the country persuaded Americans to vote them into office. Now comes the hard part: Convincing those who didn’t trust them to believe in their mission. https://t.co/uzaevvYlbH", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120905803393585340"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-12T15:37:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120903695315382287"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "In this edition of STAT Health Tech: Oura's big bet on AI, a 'rumble strip' for clinical chatbots, and questions around Medicare’s AI prior-auth experiment.", "display_url": "trib.al/KuvlkUP", "end": 180, "expanded_url": "https://trib.al/KuvlkUP", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120903700218589184/CSX94npd?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120903700218589184/CSX94npd?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 157, "status": 200, "title": "New documents raise more questions about Medicare’s AI prior-authorization experiment", "unwound_url": "ht